{
  "id": "fluency-l6-completing-the-square",
  "course": "quadratics",
  "lesson": "l6-completing-the-square",
  "title": "Fluency: completing the square",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 12,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "find-the-constant",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "complete the square",
      "vars": {
        "h": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-12, 12] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t", "r"] }
      },
      "let": { "b": "2*h", "h2": "h^2", "k": "c - h^2", "b2": "4*h^2" },
      "where": ["c != h2"],
      "prompt": "Write ${poly(v; 1, b, c)} = ({v}{h:+})^2 + q$. What is $q$?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{k}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "added-corner", "value": "{c + h2}", "line": "You added the corner ${h2}$: the square $({v}{h:+})^2$ already holds it, so take it away." },
        { "id": "b-not-halved", "value": "{c - b2}", "line": "You took away ${b:()}^2$: the corner is half of ${b}$, squared, which is ${h2}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Half of ${b}$ is ${h}$, and ${h:()}^2 = {h2}$.",
        "So ${poly(v; 1, b, 0)} = ({v}{h:+})^2 - {h2}$.",
        "Adding ${c}$ gives $q = {c} - {h2} = {k}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "solve-by-square",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "solve by completing the square",
      "vars": {
        "h": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "k": { "int": [1, 7] },
        "w": { "pick": ["smaller", "larger"] },
        "g": { "pick": [-1, 1] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "b": "-2*h", "c": "h^2 - k^2", "h2": "h^2", "k2": "k^2", "r": "h + g*k", "other": "h - g*k", "lo": "h - k", "hi": "h + k", "nh": "-h" },
      "where": ["(w == 'larger' and g == 1) or (w == 'smaller' and g == -1)", "k != abs(h)", "-h + g*k != h - g*k"],
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; 1, b, c)} = 0$ by completing the square. What is the {w} root?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{r}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "other-root", "value": "{other}", "line": "That is the other root: the question asks for the {w} one." },
        { "id": "centre-sign", "value": "{-h + g*k}", "line": "The square is $({v}{nh:+})^2$, so the roots sit either side of ${h}$, not ${nh}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Half of ${b}$ is ${nh}$, so ${poly(v; 1, b, c)} = ({v}{nh:+})^2 -{h2}{c:+} = ({v}{nh:+})^2 - {k2}$.",
        "Then $({v}{nh:+})^2 = {k2}$, so ${v}{nh:+} = \\pm {k}$.",
        "The roots are ${lo}$ and ${hi}$; the {w} is ${r}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "largest-value",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "find the largest value from the square form",
      "vars": {
        "h": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-20, 10] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "q", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "b": "2*h", "h2": "h^2", "top": "c + h^2", "nh": "-h" },
      "where": ["top != h", "c - h2 != h", "c != 0"],
      "prompt": "Complete the square on ${poly(v; -1, b, c)}$. What is its largest value?",
      "widget": { "kind": "numeric", "answer": "{top}", "tol": { "abs": 0 } },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "corner-sign", "value": "{c - h2}", "line": "Taking out the minus turns $-{h2}$ into $+{h2}$: the largest value is ${c} + {h2}$." },
        { "id": "gave-the-input", "value": "{h}", "line": "That is the value of ${v}$ where it is largest; the question asks for the largest value itself." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "${poly(v; -1, b, c)} = -({poly(v; 1, -b, 0)}){c:+} = -\\big(({v}{nh:+})^2 - {h2}\\big){c:+}$.",
        "That is ${top} - ({v}{nh:+})^2$, and a square is never negative.",
        "So the largest value is ${top}$, when ${v} = {h}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
